WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.370
“SCP-682 must be destroyed as soon as possible.”

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:11.150
So begins the SCP Foundation file on the dreaded
SCP - 682, a highly-intelligent reptilian

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:16.760
monster that has - despite the Foundation’s
best efforts - proved impossible to kill.

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.400
It may not be the most dangerous SCP out there,
considering that some are capable of eliminating

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.880
entire realities, but it’s one of the most
iconic, and you’ve probably heard tales

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:30.770
of the monster that death forgot, and you
know exactly why everyone is so afraid of

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:33.030
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.969
It’s been subjected to some of the most
deadly weapons and traps the Foundation could

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:41.780
devise, and survived attacks from some of
its deadliest fellow SCPs.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.589
But before we tell you about the Foundation’s
many failed assassination attempts against

00:00:45.589 --> 00:00:50.280
the so-called “Hard to Kill Reptile”,
we need a little more groundwork on what this

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.829
creature even is.

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:56.770
The first thing to know about SCP - 682, is
that this thing wants you and everyone you

00:00:56.770 --> 00:00:58.870
know dead.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:04.710
Unlike some other creatures like SCP - 096
and SCP - 173, which are murderous but exhibit

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:11.270
no real higher processing skills, SCP - 682
possesses cunning, advanced reasoning, and

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.590
even human-level logical intelligence.

00:01:13.590 --> 00:01:19.020
SCP - 682 can engage you in conversation,
but just talking to the creature calmly and

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.190
cordially will sometimes cause it to enter
its “rage state” where it becomes even

00:01:23.190 --> 00:01:25.170
more dangerous and volatile.

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:29.580
The beast is perpetually kept in a huge tank
of powerful hydrochloric acid, melting its

00:01:29.580 --> 00:01:33.939
tissue to prevent it from reaching its full
potential and going on a rampage.

00:01:33.939 --> 00:01:38.579
The creature’s most terrifying asset, and
the reason it’s proven impossible to terminate

00:01:38.579 --> 00:01:44.100
thus far, is its incredible adaptability to
any and all external stimuli.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:50.539
682 is a reactive being, capable of not only
surviving and regenerating from all attacks,

00:01:50.539 --> 00:01:53.939
but often incorporating those attacks into
its own wide arsenal.

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:58.399
In other words, if you’re hoping to kill
this thing, you better kill it on the first

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:04.210
hit - cause if you don’t, you better believe
it’s gonna hit you back a hundred times

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.640
harder.

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.100
This brings us to the main event: Some of
the SCP Foundation’s most ambitious and

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:15.880
frightening attempts to terminate SCP - 682,
or even understand how it could theoretically

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.440
be terminated.

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:21.441
There are quite literally too many unsuccessful
attempts for us to list them all here, so

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:25.510
think of this as a highlight reel of the Foundation’s
most prominent failures.

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:31.270
682 was first cross-tested with SCP - 017,
a humanoid shadow-entity shown to be able

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:35.680
to consume matter with its shadows and leave
no traces behind.

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:41.340
Tests on tissue samples from 682 showed that
SCP - 017 was able to consume said tissues

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:43.150
with no adverse effects.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:49.170
However, when SCP - 017 was placed into the
containment chamber with the actual creature,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:54.350
682 let out a horrific roar that was so loud
it damaged nearby audio equipment.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:03:00.290
SCP - 017 fled to the corner of the room,
and 682, in its rage state, attempted to breach

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:02.020
containment.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:06.780
Agents managed to suppress and remove the
creature, but no meaningful damage was logged.

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.780
Attempt failed.

00:03:07.780 --> 00:03:13.360
SCP - 173 - the Killer statue - was later
brought in, hoping that its thus-far impeccable

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.940
track recording for killing would hold strong.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:20.940
The second that 173 was introduced into the
testing area, 682 retreated to the far wall

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:23.090
and began screeching intensely.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:25.600
It was intelligent enough to know what it
was dealing with here.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:30.030
While the researchers and guards expected
an instantaneous reaction, there was actually

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:35.870
a stalemate for over six hours as 682 stared
at 173 continuously.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:40.680
Eventually, the tie was broken when Agents
shot out 682’s eyes with high-caliber sniper

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.660
rifles, breaking the line of sight and causing
173 to attack.

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.230
Though 682 sustained damage to several parts
of its body while its eyes regenerated, the

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.960
creature was not killed.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:56.070
It then regenerated a number of eyes all over
its body, covered in a clear, armoured carapace

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.380
that made them resistant to bullets.

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:03.160
The stalemate continued for an additional
twelve hours, as 682 maintained perpetual

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.210
eye contact.

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:08.910
173 was eventually removed from the containment
unit, and the mission was aborted.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:10.040
Attempt failed.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:15.480
In their desperation, the SCP Foundation resorted
to bringing in another dangerous and seemingly

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:23.040
unkillable monster to take on 682: SCP - 096,
also known as The Shy Guy.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:28.540
As astute SCP fans will already know, this
being kills anything that sees its face, with

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:33.780
no known exceptions - and when it enters its
attack mode, it’s thought to be quite literally

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:34.780
unstoppable.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:38.100
Or, at least, it was.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:44.840
While SCP - 096 was able to destroy 85% of
682’s original body mass during their 27

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:50.850
hour battle, it was left mentally broken - wounded,
and huddled in the corner.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:56.460
To this day, if ever confronted with SCP 682,
the Shy Guy reacts in pure terror, turning

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:59.210
away and clawing at his own face.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.460
Attempt failed.

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:06.650
During a deadly containment breach, SCP - 682
also went head to head organically with another

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:13.050
iconic SCP hall-of-famer: SCP - 106, also
known as The Old Man.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:19.360
The Old Man and a shapeshifting, psionic anomaly
known as SCP - 953 broke into 682’s containment

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:20.360
cell.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:24.480
The Old Man pulled both of his fellow anomalous
combatants into his pocket dimension to continue

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:25.960
the battle on his terms.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:31.700
However, despite losing 67% of his body mass
during the ensuing pocket dimension showdown,

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:37.810
682 still prevailed - with the Old Man eventually
fleeing back to his cell, and 953 being collected

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.700
and taken away by agents.

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:43.810
Once again, SCP - 682 continued to hold the
title.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:47.840
But it wasn’t just cross-testing experiments,
intentional or otherwise.

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:52.890
The SCP Foundation’s quest to kill 682 lead
them to a number of more conventional murder

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.380
methods, all with varying degrees of success.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:06:01.930
Due to SCP - 682’s highly adaptive abilities,
some methods were discounted from the outset.

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:06.169
For example, launching a powerful thermonuclear
missile at the creature was soundly rejected

00:06:06.169 --> 00:06:10.400
by O5 Command - on the premise that, if the
creature wasn’t destroyed and evolved to

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:15.380
the point where it could shrug off nukes,
humanity would be pretty much done for.

00:06:15.380 --> 00:06:19.210
Other ideas were abandoned just for being
too ridiculous - such as one researcher’s

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.740
suggestion to fly the creature through the
air and drop it from a considerable height,

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:24.870
hoping to kill it with the high-altitude impact.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:28.450
I’m not sure we even need to tell you why
that’s a terrible idea.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:33.900
But, during the experiments on SCP - 682,
the studies ranged from honest to incompetent

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.710
to straight-up evil.

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:40.790
One guest researcher fed two small, innocent
children to the creature, just to see what

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:41.790
would happen.

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:45.490
He was then himself fed to the creature for
his sadistic behaviour, which was viewed as

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:48.300
getting in the way of his professional conduct.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:51.840
After all, the Foundation is meant to be cold,
not cruel.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:55.449
It was SCP - 682 that had the monopoly on
cruelty.

00:06:55.449 --> 00:06:58.010
Memetic Kill agents were a resounding failure.

00:06:58.010 --> 00:07:02.720
They attempted to dismember 682 with a powerful
laser, only to have the creature develop reflective

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.530
surfaces that displaced the beam and caused
catastrophic damage to the area around it.

00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:11.370
They attempted to kill the creature by sucking
all the air out of its containment facility

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:16.730
and creating a vacuum, but it expelled a dangerous
gaseous compound that reacted violently and

00:07:16.730 --> 00:07:20.010
exploded when air was once again introduced
into the room.

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:26.120
The Foundation used high-precision blades
to slice SCP - 682 into approximately 12,000

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:28.690
pieces then separated these pieces.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:31.910
Unsurprisingly by this point, this attempt
also failed.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:36.420
The 12,000 pieces reformed a short while later
into the fully operational killing machine

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.980
we all know and fear.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:42.430
In one particularly frightening display of
intelligence and adaptability, the Foundation

00:07:42.430 --> 00:07:47.330
attempted to kill 682 with extreme heat, but
it shielded itself by developing a secondary

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.960
carapace composed of solid helium.

00:07:49.960 --> 00:07:53.490
When personnel entered the room following
the failed attempt on the creature’s life,

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:58.389
it shattered its helium carapace into deadly
shards that fired around the room and shredded

00:07:58.389 --> 00:08:01.080
all Foundation personnel in attendance.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:05.370
It’d set a trap, and that trap had been
wildly successful.

00:08:05.370 --> 00:08:09.729
The creature’s ability to adapt to seemingly
any offensive is unparalleled, to the point

00:08:09.729 --> 00:08:14.780
where Foundation staff have no idea how to
classify this creature - whether it’s organic,

00:08:14.780 --> 00:08:19.990
inorganic, or even alive at all based on any
definitions we could understand.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:23.080
At every turn, the creature just raised more
questions.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.080
What is it?

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:26.800
Is it possible to destroy it at all by any
means?

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:29.120
Who was even trying to kill who here?

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:34.550
Because it certainly seemed like SCP - 682
had a masterful K/D ratio by now.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:38.599
More extreme feats of cross-testing continued
in the Foundation’s growing desperation

00:08:38.599 --> 00:08:40.589
to eliminate this monster.

00:08:40.589 --> 00:08:46.240
SCP - 162, which is a hypnotic ball of sharp
objects, hooks, and high-tension fishing line,

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.730
was introduced to 682’s containment cell.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:53.220
The hooks latched onto the creature and tore
huge portions off, including its entire lower

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.190
jaw and one of its limbs.

00:08:55.190 --> 00:09:02.170
However, 682 was still able to breach containment,
kill eleven people, and badly wound 86 others.

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.370
It regenerated its severe injuries in no time.

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:09.360
The beast was even taken to the domain of
The Gate Guardian, one of the proposals for

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:11.160
SCP - 001.

00:09:11.160 --> 00:09:15.740
The Guardian has a flaming sword hotter than
the sun, capable of destroying its targets

00:09:15.740 --> 00:09:17.529
on an atomic level.

00:09:17.529 --> 00:09:21.879
Naturally, SCP - 682 survived and regenerated.

00:09:21.879 --> 00:09:28.970
Perhaps the most fascinating cross-test of
all was between 682 and SCP - 053, who manifests

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:33.880
as a kind, innocent little girl with the unfortunate
condition of causing homicidal tendencies

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:38.160
in all who come into contact with her for
more than ten minutes.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.649
The people with these tendencies would then
attempt to harm the girl, but would immediately

00:09:41.649 --> 00:09:45.550
drop dead shortly after, leaving the girl
intact.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:49.990
The researchers present anticipated two possible
outcomes here: The optimistic outcome, in

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:54.209
which 682 entered a rage state, attacked 053,
and died for good.

00:09:54.209 --> 00:09:59.490
And the realistic outcome, in which 682 attacked
053, possibly experienced some minor injury

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:03.879
or nothing at all, and 053 had to be removed
from the containment cell.

00:10:03.879 --> 00:10:05.339
But that didn’t happen.

00:10:05.339 --> 00:10:09.790
What did occur was considerably more shocking
than any kind of violence.

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:16.189
When 053 entered 682’s containment chamber,
the monster became uncharacteristically docile.

00:10:16.189 --> 00:10:20.920
Researchers and staff were baffled, and watched
with amazement as 053 approached the terrifying,

00:10:20.920 --> 00:10:25.679
immortal, mass-murdering monster...and began
to play with it.

00:10:25.679 --> 00:10:30.209
682 even allowed 053 to draw on its face with
crayons.

00:10:30.209 --> 00:10:34.100
Researchers thought they must’ve been dreaming,
seeing this surreal display play out.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:37.390
053 even appeared to have affection for this
unkillable misanthrope.

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:42.250
It was a single act in defiance of everything
they thought they knew.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:47.149
When Foundation personnel entered the containment
cell to separate the two, 682 went ballistic

00:10:47.149 --> 00:10:48.970
and killed multiple guards.

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:53.579
053 also wept, sad at being separated from
her new friend.

00:10:53.579 --> 00:10:59.360
To this day, despite further testing, the
Foundation has no idea how or why this happened.

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:06.220
Like many details surrounding SCP - 682, it’s
shrouded in deeply frustrating mystery.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:12.529
And so the tale of SCP - 682 continues, in
spite of the Foundation’s best efforts.

00:11:12.529 --> 00:11:17.110
The monster continues to breach containment
and slaughter with some regularity, taking

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:23.009
out its seemingly limitless hatred for not
only human beings, but anything that dares

00:11:23.009 --> 00:11:24.559
draw breath.

00:11:24.559 --> 00:11:29.350
Nobody knows where exactly the creature is
from, what its true nature is, or why its

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:34.459
ability to adapt and regenerate far exceeds
any known organism on this planet.

00:11:34.459 --> 00:11:39.220
Perhaps one day, through enough research and
cross testing, we can someday answer these

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:46.829
questions with scientific precision, but until
then, we only have one answer: Hatred never

00:11:46.829 --> 00:11:47.579
dies.

